{"kind":"report","text":"G0b/G1 prerequisite decision against Main b686384a813b7ed607ec88ee263cc4fb27157998. Approve proceeding to a separately reviewed internal G0b Source slice under these conditions; this report approves no Source or adapter switch.\n\nG0b: feed the existing platform editTree with verified base commit plus the complete bodies of only the ancestor directories needed by the explicit edit paths. Do not fork the editor or inspect only selected rows of a returned tree. Verify object ID/type/size and strictly parse each fetched commit/tree before using edges; editTree's private treeRows is a permissive editor decoder, not an untrusted-object validator. Reader's commit/tree checks provide existing SHA1 consumer semantics; do not claim SHA256 transport support from editTree's format parameter because current isolated transport/Reader is SHA1. Any other format must be explicit unsupported until its parser/hash/transport are delivered.\n\nValidate the whole path cohort before I/O: reuse editPath, at most64 distinct paths, whole-cohort file/folder conflicts, UTF8 byte lengths, explicit depth and aggregate path/work limits, and no distinct strings aliasing the same encoded path. Non-well-formed Unicode needs refusal rather than replacement-byte aliasing. Bytewise compare tree names; unrelated non-UTF8 names remain unchanged bytes. Preserve100644/100755 at replaced leaves; refuse traversed symlink/gitlink or file-directory conflict. A missing child is known only after successfully validating the complete containing tree. A denied/missing/corrupt requested object, unsupported isolated capability or exhausted bound refuses the retrieval whole, never proves an absent path. Existing isolated mode's refusal must not trigger full-closure fallback.\n\nBound distinct object requests, per-kind size, retained output bytes and aggregate ownership before requesting: reserve the maximum permitted next object allowance, pass the remaining bound to the source, then charge actual verified bytes. Compose the retrieval's buffers/copies with the isolated source's ownedBytes, cache/lifetime output reservations and deadline/terminal behavior. No unbounded retry/concurrent fan-out. Shared ancestor IDs may deduplicate, but an expected-type conflict refuses. Explicit partial result, no closure=true or possession credential. Do not read parent commits, unrelated child bodies, or the old leaf blob merely to overwrite it; new path suffixes require no further source reads after verified absence.\n\nWitnesses for the Source slice: exact requested object set for shared/nested/new paths; large unrelated blob/subtree and deep commit ancestry never requested; changed result equals existing editTree and real local Git for supported format; preserved executable/regular modes; symlink/gitlink/file-folder refusal; malformed/duplicate/out-of-order tree rows and hash/type refusal; missing/denied selected tree never absent; path/object/payload boundaries and terminal timeout cannot produce partial success. Keep fixtures local/finite and clearly distinguish real Git readback from a synthetic transport transcript.\n\nG1: a witness needs TWO independent facts: verified closure content under the selected validation policy, and current possession/retention of that exact closure by the exact destination repository. Store these separately, with immutable repository identity plus authenticated host/service/namespace and repository generation, object format/base ID, proof origin/version and validity/invalidation rules. Name/URL, a ref advertisement, a fetched base commit or G0b success proves neither full closure nor retention. No bearer secret belongs in this witness.\n\nFor imported repositories, retain an initial complete verified-closure certificate once (or a separately adopted trustworthy host-connectivity attestation, explicitly a different trust basis); a bounded walk that has not finished is not this certificate. Maintain possession through an authorized retained root/ref with a defined host retention guarantee, or a transaction-scoped verified host guarantee covering the send. Ref existence observed once is not a lease. Renames/transfers/recreation, broken retention, deletion, revocation, changed validation policy or unbound host/repository identity invalidate reuse unless the contract proves otherwise. If a host exposes no adequate retention guarantee and no current verifiable proof, G1 is unavailable there; do not manufacture a constant-time local proof. The import plan must expose that prerequisite or unfinished bounded verification, rather than claim arbitrary imported histories supported.\n\nThe certificate can advance inductively after a fully verified delta publication and its required evidence: verify/hash every new object and all its edges; omit only edges proved reachable from the certified base via verified tree/commit paths, preserving expected type. A list of arbitrary existing IDs or one commit stop is not sufficient for unchanged tree siblings. This avoids enumerating base history on every edit while retaining the original complete-content premise. No unrelated host object or alternate repository can borrow the certificate. Retention must remain valid at the actual send boundary, not only while planning.\n\nCurrent sendOnce stops commit ancestry at old but still walks the new tree closure; inspectGit checks both full closures, full trees and report ancestry. Thus G0b cannot replace DestinationProvider.objects at those consumers. Future G1 needs an explicit typed proof-consuming send boundary and separately reviewed inspection/change-set/ancestry policy; it must not simply widen Reader.closure stops or return partial objects from the complete provider contract. First-head/checker/staging gates remain unchanged.\n\nProtocol evidence: Git receive-pack normally checks reachable connectivity; its skip-connectivity option requires a reliable external mechanism (https://git-scm.com/docs/git-receive-pack). Git GC's retention is based on referenced/recent objects, so cached identity alone is not ongoing custody (https://git-scm.com/docs/git-gc). Pack ref updates compare old IDs at processing time (https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-pack); this CAS does not by itself establish our local validation policy. Own complete push answer plus readback stays required for accepted; lost/incomplete reply remains unknown, and nothing here authorizes retry.\n\nExact static consumers read: platform destination-objects/editPath/editTree, scope provider objects, destination-host inspect/build paths, github-host sendOnce/inspectGit and Git Reader parsers/closure. No project execution or host operation. Parent e029 remains open.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e7d78f9574856033a8a5c60a1a104ef3c32a635","scope":"pre-Source G0b/G1 prerequisite decision"}}